==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|því}}, possibly from the instrumental interrogative {{der|is|gem-pro|*hwī||how, with what}}, with the initial h- replaced by the þ- from the forms of {{m|gem-pro|*sa}}.

===Conjunction===
{{head|is|conjunction}}

# [[because]], [[for]], [[since]]
#* Colossians 3:9
#*: {{ux|is|Ljúgið ekki hver að öðrum, '''því''' þér hafið afklæðst hinum gamla manni með gjörðum hans.|Do not lie to each other, '''since''' you have taken off your old self with its practices.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|af því að}}, {{l|is|því að||because}}
* {{l|is|því aðeins að||only if, on the condition that}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun}}

# {{label|is|personal}} {{inflection of|það||dat|s|lang=is}}

====Declension====
{{Icelandic personal pronouns}}

===Adverb===
{{is-adv|head=því...því}}

# [[the]]...[[the]] (when comparing)
#: {{ux|is|en '''því''' meira sem hann blés, '''því''' þéttara vafði ferðamaðurinn kápunni að sér|but '''the''' more he blew, '''the''' tighter the traveller wrapped his coat around himself}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|því miður}}

